    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag following the same pattern the codebase already uses for `bulkSignupWarning`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only boolean `capacityWarning` field to the `OwnerDto` schema, so the generated DTO gets a `setCapacityWarning`/`getCapacityWarning` accessor.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct doesn't complain about the unmapped target (the controller populates it explicitly, like `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant and an `isCityApproachingCapacity(String city)` helper. It counts owners in the city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed \u2014 matching the existing `isCityAtCapacity` normalization) and returns `true` when the count is in `[40, 49]` (i.e. `>= 40 && < CITY_CAPACITY`).\n   - Set `capacityWarning` at every point where `bulkSignupWarning` is set: `getOwner`, `listOwners` (per owner), `addOwner`, the idempotent-create path, and `updateOwner`.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`isCityAtCapacity` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`) is untouched, so the two boundaries stay consistent: 40\u201349 warns, 50+ rejects.",
